{
  "$comment": [
    "The author's own 3-day muscle-gain program, as given: 21 + 20 + 20 = 61 working sets a week.",
    "",
    "Exercises are named by catalog SLUG, not id. seed-program.sh resolves them against",
    "GET /api/exercises at run time, so this file stays readable and survives a reseeded database.",
    "",
    "percentOfWorking is a FRACTION, not a percentage: the domain requires 0 < p < 1, so 53% is",
    "0.53. Where the program gave a range (40-50%), the midpoint is used, because a prescription",
    "holds one number per warm-up step. Percentages must increase strictly from step to step.",
    "",
    "Rest is in seconds, min and max. The program's own REST section overrides the per-exercise",
    "line where the two disagree -- e.g. bench says 'dam 3 min' in the exercise list and '2.5-3",
    "min' in the REST table, so 150-180 is used.",
    "",
    "One thing this file CANNOT express faithfully: Back Squat's first warm-up is 'bo'sh shtanga",
    "(odatda 20 kg)' -- an absolute weight, not a fraction of the working weight. Warm-up steps are",
    "percentages only, so 0.25 stands in for it. At a 100 kg squat that resolves to 25 kg rather",
    "than the bar's 20 kg. Adjust the number to taste, or log that first set by hand."
  ],
